#alert-text([To park a request and multiplex the thread, the future must own its buffer and message.])


// Slide 7
== Storing the Resumable State

#v(1em)
#side-by-side[
  #section("Data Compartment Ownership", [
    - borrowed message? #h(1fr) #cross No
    - borrowed buffer? #h(1fr) #cross No
    - DSA submission params? #h(1fr) #checkmark Yes
    - completion waker? #h(1fr) #checkmark Yes
  ])
][
  #section("Tonic Storage Boundary", [
    The driver stores the owned future in `EncodedBytes::in_flight`.

    Since the stack-frame is long gone, the future keeps all progress, data, and hardware descriptors alive.
  ])
]

#v(2em)
#alert-text([The future must own all data compartments to safely survive suspension crossing `.await`.])


// Slide 8
== Synthesis: How it Works

#v(1em)
#side-by-side[
  #section("1. Encode Suspends", [
    When waiting for hardware copies, the encoder yields `Pending`, freeing the CPU thread to handle other streams.
  ])
][
  #section("2. Driver Multiplexes", [
    Tonic's body driver stores the owned future, polling it when the hardware waker signals completion.
  ])
]

#v(2.2em)
#section("Resumable State", [
  Prost records exact wire-format resume positions (tag written, length written, payload copy checkpoint) to resume encoding correctly on the next poll.
])

